## Code Example

```javascript
// Circuit breaker around identity provider
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold = 5, timeout = 3000) {
    this.failureCount = 0;
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.timeout = timeout;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
    this.lastFailure = null;
  }

  async execute(operation) {
    if (this.state === 'OPEN') {
      if (Date.now() - this.lastFailure > this.timeout) {
        this.state = 'HALF_OPEN';
      } else {
        throw new Error('Circuit breaker is OPEN');
      }
    }

    try {
      const result = await operation();
      this.onSuccess();
      return result;
    } catch (error) {
      this.onFailure();
      throw error;
    }
  }

  onSuccess() {
    this.failureCount = 0;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
  }

  onFailure() {
    this.failureCount++;
    this.lastFailure = Date.now();
    if (this.failureCount >= this.threshold) {
      this.state = 'OPEN';
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design automated degradation with controlled risk during external dependency pressure and multi-region operation.

## Key Concepts
- Circuit breakers and failover
- Per-region degradation strategies
- Idempotent queues and exactly-once delivery
- Canary and synthetic testing
- Rollback criteria and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for circuit breaker state machine
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold, resetTime) {
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.resetTime = resetTime;
    this.failures = 0;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
  }
  onFailure() {
    this.failures++;
    if (this.failures > this.threshold) this.state = 'OPEN';
  }
  canRequest() { return this.state !== 'OPEN'; }
}
```

